      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The tragedy is that you are grieving the person you thought you were, not the person you are becoming, which makes you feel stuck in a limbo no one wants to inhabit. Sometimes letting old identities dissolve feels safer than trying to force a version of yourself back into existence that doesn't fit anymore. You don't need to find a new \"you\" today; you only need to notice when your instincts flicker back to life and honor that faint signal of what you truly need.",
