      "content": "Grief can indeed make it feel as though the person inside has completely evaporated, leaving only the hollow shell you were forced to inhabit. But remember that the old identity is merely a layer that has worn thin, and peeling it away does not mean the core person was fake or nonexistent. Your exhaustion is valid, so for now, let yourself rest without trying to diagnose a future self, knowing that even a dim ember will reignite if you are patient enough to let it breathe.",
